## Why This Is Asked
Tests system design skills for production AI systems, understanding of trade-offs between accuracy and latency, and knowledge of evaluation metrics in real-world scenarios.

## Expected Answer
Strong candidates will discuss: 1) Multi-stage evaluation architecture, 2) Confidence threshold tuning, 3) Fallback strategies, 4) Monitoring and alerting, 5) Cost optimization through early filtering.

## Code Example
```typescript
class HallucinationDetector {
  async evaluate(response: string, context: string) {
    const semanticScore = await this.semanticCheck(response, context);
    if (semanticScore > 0.9) return { confident: true, score: semanticScore };

    const factualScore = await this.factualVerification(response);
    const ensembleScore = this.ensembleWeighting(semanticScore, factualScore);

    return {
      confident: ensembleScore > 0.85,
      score: ensembleScore,
      needsReview: ensembleScore < 0.7
    };
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle edge cases where the knowledge graph is incomplete?
- What metrics would you track to optimize the confidence thresholds?
- How would you design A/B testing for new detection algorithms?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests production-grade RAG design across multilingual, heterogeneous corpora with multi-tenant isolation and performance constraints at scale.

## Key Concepts
- Hierarchical chunking (document → sections → paragraphs) with size optimization
- Multilingual embeddings and incremental refresh pipelines
- Vector DB partitioning with ACLs per tenant
- Two-stage retrieval with semantic search and cross-encoder reranking
- Freshness management, latency budgets (200-500ms), and comprehensive failover strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Implementation sketch for chunking and indexing
function chunkDocument(text, maxBytes = 4000) {
  const chunks = [];
  let current = '';

  // Split by paragraphs and respect semantic boundaries
  const paragraphs = text.split(/\n\s*\n/);

  for (const paragraph of paragraphs) {
    if (current.length + paragraph.length > maxBytes) {
      if (current) chunks.push(current.trim());
      current = paragraph;
    } else {
      current += (current ? '\n\n' : '') + paragraph;
    }
  }

  if (current) chunks.push(current.trim());
  return chunks;
}

// Tenant-aware retrieval
async function retrieveChunks(query, tenantId, limit = 5) {
  const embeddedQuery = await embedQuery(query);
  const results = await vectorStore.search({
    vector: embeddedQuery,
    filter: { tenantId },
    limit: limit * 2 // Get more for reranking
  });

  // Rerank with cross-encoder
  return await rerank(query, results).slice(0, limit);
}
```
